ays honored it  and uh you know so and maybe i shouldn't  have said it because now this is going  to get like distributed to all the  coaches in the nfl and they're going to  say yeah  only um you know  how about this michelle you have to have  a super bowl win  to be able to ask for this how's that  oh yeah let's suppose they're putting  all kinds of restrictions on this thing  that's great  no i think there probably is something  contractual because they do it for every  network they you know they and they do  it for their  usually they do it for their home radio  people too so  um it's there are moments  you're not gonna get hit a home run  every every half time but there are  moments when you get one  and uh you go oh gosh this is great you  know  i always refer back to bill parcells  telling me he was gonna  start tony romo in the second half and  and that was a big big news story so  i was grateful for that one have fun and  uh  you know i i'm rooting for snow i don't  know if you are but  you know fred godelli is oh you know yes  you know he is because there's this  sense that if people see snow  they will stop with their put their  remote down and watch so  yeah but michelle's gonna watch me fred  goodelli  and you know is one of the great  producers uh in  in in this business he's in a truck yes  i know that  so he's not i mean he's rooting for snow  but he he's  he doesn't care about those in the  elements  he just wants it these are pretty  pictures you know what i hear in my ear  every time it's always 70 and perfect  inside the truck and  you know the things i want to say  it's not pretty uh thank you michelle  have fun we'll be watching we appreciate  it as always  thanks dan talk to you later that's  michelle tafoya nbc sunday night  football sideline reporter  but she'll be there on saturday night


